  "answer": "I'll start by reading the debugging skill so the investigation follows that process, then look at how special prices with dates reach the storefront API.The storefront price check treats a special as active only when the start date is both before and after today, and product create writes the end date into the start-date field. I'll add tests that show both failures, then fix them.Special prices that included an end date never reached the storefront as a discount. Creating a product stored that end date in the special start-date field, and the price calculator then required the start date to be both before and after today, so a dated special could never apply. The end date is now saved on the end-date field, and the calculator applies the special when the start date has passed and the end date is still ahead.\n\nVERIFICATION: {\"ran\": [\"mvn -pl sm-core,sm-shop -am test -Dtest=ProductPriceUtilsSpecialPriceTest,PersistableProductAvailabilityMapperTest -DfailIfNoTests=false\"], \"result\": \"passed\", \"could_not_verify\": [\"storefront HTTP API against a running Shopizer instance\"], \"missing\": [\"an existing integration test that creates a product through the admin REST API and reads it from the storefront API\"]}",
